  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does Voyage AI offer that other embedding providers don't?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Voyage AI focuses exclusively on embeddings and reranking, and is the only major provider to release production-grade MoE embedding models (voyage-4-large). The voyage-4 series beats OpenAI v3 Large by 14.05%, Cohere Embed v4 by 8.20%, and Gemini Embedding 001 by 3.87% on Voyage's RTEB benchmark (29 datasets, January 2026). It also offers Matryoshka flexible dimensions (2048/1024/512/256) and the longest commercial context (32K tokens vs OpenAI's 8K)." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is the Voyage AI API OpenAI-compatible?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Voyage uses its own API contract at https://api.voyageai.com/v1/ with three endpoints: POST /v1/embeddings, POST /v1/rerank, and POST /v1/multimodalembeddings. The request schema requires an input_type parameter (query or document) which OpenAI's API does not. Authentication is Bearer token. There is no chat completions endpoint — Voyage is embedding + rerank only, not a general LLM provider." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does Voyage AI cost in 2026?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "As of June 2026, voyage-4-large is $0.12 per million tokens, voyage-4 is $0.06/M, voyage-4-lite is $0.02/M, voyage-context-3 and voyage-code-3 are $0.18/M, and voyage-multimodal-3.5 is $0.12/M text tokens plus $0.60 per billion pixels. Rerank-2.5 is $0.05/M tokens and rerank-2.5-lite is $0.02/M tokens. A 33% batch discount is available with 12-hour SLA. New accounts receive 200M free tokens for embeddings and rerankers, and 50M free tokens for legacy domain models." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does Voyage AI work from inside China?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Voyage's marketing site is reachable from China, but the company has not published any mainland-China-specific API endpoint, ICP filing, or CDN node. The official solution for restricted regions is in-VPC deployment via AWS Marketplace or Azure Marketplace, putting compute behind the customer's own cloud tenant. For teams that need a guaranteed China-direct embedding API, aggregators like FreeModel (freemodel.dev/invite/FRE-7a3b6220) bundle multiple embedding providers behind one key with verified domestic connectivity." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the difference between voyage-4-large, voyage-4, and voyage-4-lite?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "All three share the same 32K context window and 1024 default embedding dimension, and crucially share an embedding space — you can index documents with voyage-4-large and query with voyage-4-lite for asymmetric retrieval without re-indexing. voyage-4-large uses Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) for frontier accuracy at $0.12/M; voyage-4 is the mid-size balanced option at $0.06/M; voyage-4-lite is optimized for lowest latency and cost at $0.02/M. The shared embedding space is unique to Voyage — OpenAI's text-embedding-3-small and 3-large do not share a space, so asymmetric retrieval is not possible." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the RTEB benchmark and how does it differ from MTEB?",
